|> Exercise
    handle=_define_abs_val_by_cases_
    How can you define the absolute value
    function using “definition by cases”?

    |> Solution

        The absolute value function is

        $$
        x \ra \begin{cases} x & \te{if $x \geq 0$,}\\ -x\!\!\up{1.2} & \te{if $x < 0$}\end{cases}
        $$

        because $-(-1) = 1$, $-(-5) = 5$, etc.
